1
00:00:04,370 --> 00:00:05,420
Hello?

2
00:00:05,580 --> 00:00:08,630
It's me. I know you can't stand to be in the same room.

3
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:11,550
I just thought I'd try and apologize over the phone...

4
00:00:16,510 --> 00:00:18,100
Hello?

5
00:00:19,010 --> 00:00:22,180
Look, I never should've kissed your girlfriend, and I'm...

6
00:00:26,060 --> 00:00:27,100
Stop calling!

7
00:00:27,270 --> 00:00:31,280
Hey, hey, hey. This is 92.3 WXRK K-Rock...

8
00:00:31,440 --> 00:00:34,280
...calling with our $1000 daily challenge.

9
00:00:34,450 --> 00:00:35,700
All right.

10
00:00:35,860 --> 00:00:37,070
What is the name of...

11
00:00:37,240 --> 00:00:41,870
...your roommate who is very, very sorry and would do anything...?

12
00:01:30,040 --> 00:01:31,840
Ugh, turkey.

13
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:35,340
Ugh, giving thanks. Ugh.

14
00:01:35,720 --> 00:01:38,630
Look, everyone, it's the spirit of Thanksgiving.

15
00:01:39,470 --> 00:01:41,140
Are things with Joey any better?

16
00:01:41,300 --> 00:01:44,100
They couldn't be worse. I spent eight hours calling him...

17
00:01:44,270 --> 00:01:46,140
...trying to get him to talk to me.

18
00:01:46,310 --> 00:01:49,140
Oh, wow. Eight hours.

19
00:01:49,310 --> 00:01:52,980
So you could probably really use one of those plug-in telephone headsets, huh?

20
00:01:53,150 --> 00:01:57,610
Should we all expect Christmas gifts that can be stolen from your office?

21
00:02:00,070 --> 00:02:01,370
You shouldn't.

22
00:02:03,200 --> 00:02:04,490
Speaking of Christmas...

23
00:02:04,660 --> 00:02:08,660
...since Monica and I are starting a new business and have like no money...

24
00:02:08,830 --> 00:02:12,670
...this year maybe we could do Secret Santa and then we each only buy one gift.

25
00:02:12,840 --> 00:02:16,920
And there's the added mystery of, you know, who gets who.

26
00:02:18,840 --> 00:02:20,220
Who gets "whom."

27
00:02:22,390 --> 00:02:24,560
I don't know why I do that.

28
00:02:27,890 --> 00:02:31,190
Oh, I'm gonna take a nap. Turkey makes me sleepy.

29
00:02:31,350 --> 00:02:33,230
We haven't eaten yet.

30
00:02:33,900 --> 00:02:38,030
I know, but all that work you're doing to get it ready, and I just...

31
00:02:40,070 --> 00:02:42,870
Hey, did either of you pick Rachel for your Secret Santa?

32
00:02:43,030 --> 00:02:46,410
- Because I wanna trade for her.     - I picked her. Oh, thank God, you want her.

33
00:02:46,580 --> 00:02:47,950
Ooh.

34
00:02:48,120 --> 00:02:50,290
Wow, why do you wanna get rid of her so badly?

35
00:02:50,460 --> 00:02:52,420
Because she exchanges every gift she gets.

36
00:02:52,580 --> 00:02:55,090
It's, like, impossible to get her something she likes.

37
00:02:55,250 --> 00:02:56,840
Come on, let's trade.

38
00:02:57,010 --> 00:02:59,800
That's not true. I got her that backpack and she loved it.

39
00:02:59,970 --> 00:03:04,340
I remember how much she was crying the day that big dog ran off with...

40
00:03:05,970 --> 00:03:08,180
There was no big dog.

41
00:03:09,100 --> 00:03:13,850
This sucks, because I already got her this briefcase and I had "R.G." put on it.

42
00:03:14,020 --> 00:03:16,360
- Her initials.     - Oh.

43
00:03:18,320 --> 00:03:21,530
Maybe you can give it to somebody else. Oh. Like Ross Geller.

44
00:03:22,280 --> 00:03:24,740
Oh, you know what, though? It's a girlie briefcase.

45
00:03:24,910 --> 00:03:28,040
Who cares? He works in a museum.

46
00:03:29,450 --> 00:03:31,870
Hey, what time is it? The big game's about to start.

47
00:03:32,040 --> 00:03:35,210
Ross and Joey aren't here. You can watch the parade if you want.

48
00:03:35,380 --> 00:03:36,960
Thanks.

49
00:03:38,170 --> 00:03:41,800
What is wrong with this freezer? Ow! Ow!

50
00:03:41,970 --> 00:03:44,970
- God, what happened?     - Oh, my God, ice just got in my eye.

51
00:03:45,140 --> 00:03:48,100
People are trying to sleep in here.

52
00:03:48,260 --> 00:03:50,270
Monica got ice in her eye and it hurts.

53
00:03:50,430 --> 00:03:53,350
- Open it up. Let me see.     - Oh, I can't. It really kills.

54
00:03:53,520 --> 00:03:55,810
Well, maybe you should put some ice on it.

55
00:03:57,480 --> 00:04:00,820
- Ooh, it looks bad.     - Maybe we should take you to a doctor.

56
00:04:00,990 --> 00:04:02,820
No, my eye doctor is Richard.

57
00:04:02,990 --> 00:04:06,110
I can't go to him when I don't have a boyfriend.

58
00:04:06,280 --> 00:04:08,830
He's really picky about his patients.

59
00:04:09,330 --> 00:04:11,910
Okay, you've gotta go. What's his office number?

60
00:04:12,080 --> 00:04:14,830
Oh, like I remember his office number.

61
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:16,500
Speed dial 7.

62
00:04:19,170 --> 00:04:22,970
Hi, yeah, I'm calling on behalf of Monica Geller's eye, and...

63
00:04:23,550 --> 00:04:26,430
Is Richard Burke in today?

64
00:04:26,590 --> 00:04:29,180
He's out of town. Does she wanna see the on-call doctor?

65
00:04:29,350 --> 00:04:32,980
- Yes.     - Yes. She's very excited about that.

66
00:04:35,980 --> 00:04:37,190
It's so cool.

67
00:04:37,360 --> 00:04:43,150
Till Monica gets back, it's like I'm head chef and I get to make all the decisions.

68
00:04:43,780 --> 00:04:46,660
Hey, hey, I thought she told you to follow the recipe exactly.

69
00:04:46,820 --> 00:04:48,870
Okay, get out of my kitchen.

70
00:04:50,450 --> 00:04:53,200
All right, okay. I think I'm making some progress with Joey.

71
00:04:53,370 --> 00:04:56,040
When I went into the apartment, he went to his bedroom...

72
00:04:56,210 --> 00:04:58,460
...but he only slammed the door once.

73
00:04:59,210 --> 00:05:02,000
I mean, yeah, he gave me the finger while doing it.

74
00:05:03,130 --> 00:05:07,680
All right, I gotta call my mom and ask her a left-handed cooking question.

75
00:05:11,470 --> 00:05:14,310
So listen, I picked Monica for Secret Santa...

76
00:05:14,480 --> 00:05:16,560
...but I'm getting her something for Hanukkah.

77
00:05:16,730 --> 00:05:17,940
You wanna switch?

78
00:05:18,100 --> 00:05:21,570
Oh, you know what? I was trying to trade for, uh, ahem, well, you.

79
00:05:24,190 --> 00:05:26,740
Really? Wow, that's so nice. What are you gonna get me?

80
00:05:26,900 --> 00:05:30,320
I don't know, R.G. I was thinking something girlie for your office.

81
00:05:32,240 --> 00:05:35,200
Yeah. Well, maybe Phoebe will switch with me.

82
00:05:35,370 --> 00:05:39,960
Then you're gonna get stuck with Rachel, and she exchanges every gift she ever gets.

83
00:05:40,130 --> 00:05:43,130
Oh, that's not true. I got her lots of stuff she never took back.

84
00:05:43,300 --> 00:05:44,500
Like?

85
00:05:44,670 --> 00:05:46,670
Like that gold necklace I got her last year.

86
00:05:47,260 --> 00:05:49,260
When was the last time you saw her wear it?

87
00:05:49,430 --> 00:05:52,930
Well, she wore it all Christmas day and then, uh...

88
00:05:54,310 --> 00:05:55,470
Big dog?

89
00:06:00,900 --> 00:06:02,110
- Hey.     - Hey.

90
00:06:02,520 --> 00:06:03,570
What are you doing?

91
00:06:03,730 --> 00:06:06,320
Sending back this stuff Chandler bought out of guilt.

92
00:06:06,900 --> 00:06:10,660
- Everything? Even the TV?     - No, I'm gonna put that in my room.

93
00:06:12,280 --> 00:06:16,450
Listen, Joey. I know what he did was wrong.

94
00:06:16,620 --> 00:06:18,870
But don't you think you could hear the guy out?

95
00:06:19,040 --> 00:06:20,750
When you and Rachel were together...

96
00:06:20,920 --> 00:06:23,420
...if Chandler had kissed her, would you hear him out?

97
00:06:23,590 --> 00:06:25,130
That's a good point.

98
00:06:26,130 --> 00:06:28,550
So how long you gonna punish him?

99
00:06:28,720 --> 00:06:30,300
Five years.

100
00:06:31,470 --> 00:06:32,510
You've sentenced him?

101
00:06:32,680 --> 00:06:35,760
Hey, don't do the crime if you can't do the time.

102
00:06:36,180 --> 00:06:39,980
- But, Joey, the guy's your best friend.     - No, was my best friend.

103
00:06:40,140 --> 00:06:42,350
I don't know why you're pushing for him so hard.

104
00:06:42,520 --> 00:06:46,070
With him out of the way as my best friend, there's a spot open.

105
00:06:48,360 --> 00:06:50,950
- Who, me?     - Yeah.

106
00:06:51,110 --> 00:06:52,990
Wow. I'm honored.

107
00:06:53,160 --> 00:06:56,080
You know what I'm gonna do as my first act as your best friend?

108
00:06:56,240 --> 00:06:58,700
I'm gonna get you to talk to Chandler.

109
00:07:00,370 --> 00:07:01,960
All right.

110
00:07:02,130 --> 00:07:04,330
Oh, but if you weren't my best friend...

111
00:07:04,500 --> 00:07:05,710
Ah.

112
00:07:07,210 --> 00:07:09,550
Oh, my God. Is it really that bad?

113
00:07:09,720 --> 00:07:12,010
I walk in the room, and he won't even talk to me.

114
00:07:12,180 --> 00:07:15,350
He just mumbles something in Italian.

115
00:07:16,350 --> 00:07:19,100
And I know he only knows the bad words.

116
00:07:23,350 --> 00:07:25,690
Hey, Gunther, have you seen Chandler?

117
00:07:26,400 --> 00:07:27,860
I thought you were Chandler.

118
00:07:30,530 --> 00:07:32,860
But, um, one of you is over there.

119
00:07:38,910 --> 00:07:39,950
Oh.

120
00:07:41,040 --> 00:07:42,460
Hey, Joe.

121
00:07:51,970 --> 00:07:53,300
I'll be right with you, okay?

122
00:07:53,840 --> 00:07:55,590
Thanks for coming in.

123
00:07:56,390 --> 00:07:59,970
Oh, my God. How cute is the on-call doctor?

124
00:08:00,140 --> 00:08:03,770
Oh. So cute that I'm thinking about jamming this pen in my eye.

125
00:08:07,270 --> 00:08:08,570
Dr. Burke will see you now.

126
00:08:08,730 --> 00:08:11,230
Oh, no, no, no, not Dr. Burke. Dr. Burke's out of town.

127
00:08:11,400 --> 00:08:13,150
The on-call doctor will see me now.

128
00:08:13,320 --> 00:08:14,910
Dr. Richard Burke is out.

129
00:08:15,070 --> 00:08:18,490
Dr. Timothy Burke, his son, will see you now.

130
00:08:19,910 --> 00:08:21,540
Ready?

131
00:08:28,420 --> 00:08:30,920
Hey, I'm sorry. That...

132
00:08:31,880 --> 00:08:34,550
- Where you going?     - My folks'.

133
00:08:34,720 --> 00:08:36,380
Oh. Uh...

134
00:08:36,550 --> 00:08:38,140
When you coming back?

135
00:08:38,300 --> 00:08:39,550
I don't know.

136
00:08:39,720 --> 00:08:42,850
I might stay there for a few days while I look for an apartment.

137
00:08:43,770 --> 00:08:44,810
What?

138
00:08:45,270 --> 00:08:48,860
Yeah, you know, at first I thought we could talk about this, work it out.

139
00:08:49,020 --> 00:08:51,270
But seeing you two together, I don't...

140
00:08:51,440 --> 00:08:55,450
Hey, look, what do you want me to say? Do you want me to say I'll stop seeing her?

141
00:08:55,610 --> 00:08:58,280
It's not about her. Okay?

142
00:08:58,450 --> 00:09:01,950
But seeing you two together just reminds me of what you did.

143
00:09:02,120 --> 00:09:05,790
And I don't wanna live with someone who doesn't know what it is to be a friend.

144
00:09:05,960 --> 00:09:09,330
- So I'll see you.     - Hey, look, I know what it is to be a friend.

145
00:09:09,500 --> 00:09:12,630
- I just... I screwed up.     - Yeah, you did.

146
00:09:13,630 --> 00:09:15,380
And that's why I'm leaving.

147
00:09:16,760 --> 00:09:20,050
Look, if you're not gonna stay for me, then at least stay for them.

148
00:09:22,220 --> 00:09:26,350
Okay? They have had a very difficult year, what with the robbery and all.

149
00:09:27,060 --> 00:09:28,520
When that guy was robbing us...

150
00:09:28,690 --> 00:09:31,570
...and I was locked in the entertainment unit for six hours...

151
00:09:31,730 --> 00:09:33,440
...do you know what I was doing?

152
00:09:33,610 --> 00:09:35,490
I was thinking about how I let you down.

153
00:09:36,780 --> 00:09:37,820
- Wow.     - Yeah.

154
00:09:37,990 --> 00:09:41,740
If I'd have known what kind of friend you were gonna be, I wouldn't have worried.

155
00:09:41,910 --> 00:09:43,870
- See you around.     - All right, wait, come on.

156
00:09:44,040 --> 00:09:47,910
Just wait one second. There has to be something that I can do.

157
00:09:48,080 --> 00:09:49,420
If we still had that unit...

158
00:09:49,580 --> 00:09:53,340
...I would get in there for six hours and think about how I let you down.

159
00:09:59,470 --> 00:10:00,680
What?

160
00:10:00,850 --> 00:10:02,010
We got a box.

161
00:10:06,350 --> 00:10:08,770
I remember the last time I saw you.

162
00:10:08,940 --> 00:10:11,480
It was the morning I left for college.

163
00:10:12,060 --> 00:10:14,860
You were just standing outside the Dairy Queen.

164
00:10:15,030 --> 00:10:18,190
Heh. Just probably waiting for it to open.

165
00:10:19,240 --> 00:10:21,030
Gotta tell you, you look great now.

166
00:10:21,660 --> 00:10:24,620
- You look great too.     - You're an excellent patient.

167
00:10:26,370 --> 00:10:27,450
So how does it look?

168
00:10:27,620 --> 00:10:31,750
You've got a little scratch on your cornea. You're gonna have to wear a patch.

169
00:10:31,920 --> 00:10:33,710
Like a pirate?

170
00:10:34,500 --> 00:10:35,630
If that helps you.

171
00:10:40,430 --> 00:10:43,470
Ahem. So how long have you been working with your dad?

172
00:10:44,600 --> 00:10:46,970
Come on, one of us had to mention him.

173
00:10:47,680 --> 00:10:49,730
I moved back here a couple months ago.

174
00:10:49,890 --> 00:10:51,060
Ah.

175
00:10:51,230 --> 00:10:53,810
- Big family dinner tonight?     - Uh...

176
00:10:54,730 --> 00:10:56,440
No way.

177
00:10:56,610 --> 00:10:58,740
I was gonna have Thanksgiving at my girlfriend's.

178
00:10:58,900 --> 00:11:00,320
- Oh.     - But we broke up.

179
00:11:00,700 --> 00:11:01,780
Oh?

180
00:11:03,320 --> 00:11:05,580
She wasn't ready for a serious commitment.

181
00:11:06,120 --> 00:11:07,410
Oh.

182
00:11:08,750 --> 00:11:11,790
So you made her walk the plank, aye, matey?

183
00:11:12,920 --> 00:11:14,460
You're not wearing the patch yet.

184
00:11:17,920 --> 00:11:19,550
I know.

185
00:11:25,300 --> 00:11:28,470
- He's coming here for Thanksgiving?     - I know. It's sick.

186
00:11:28,640 --> 00:11:31,560
- Why is it sick?     - Because it's Richard's son.

187
00:11:31,730 --> 00:11:34,310
It's like inviting a Greek tragedy over for dinner.

188
00:11:35,980 --> 00:11:38,570
I mean, come on, Phoebe, you understand, don't you?

189
00:11:38,730 --> 00:11:41,950
Yeah, I could see where I'd be your best shot, but no.

190
00:11:43,030 --> 00:11:45,700
- Sorry, honey. I think it's twisted.     - Yeah.

191
00:11:45,870 --> 00:11:48,740
- What's twisted?     - Oh. Me going out with Richard's son.

192
00:11:48,910 --> 00:11:50,450
Ew.

193
00:11:51,790 --> 00:11:53,620
Ew, ew, ew.

194
00:11:54,580 --> 00:11:56,750
It sounds like a really bad idea to me.

195
00:11:59,460 --> 00:12:00,760
Is he okay in there?

196
00:12:00,920 --> 00:12:03,340
He's fine.

197
00:12:03,930 --> 00:12:06,800
You know, if things work out between you and Richard's son...

198
00:12:06,970 --> 00:12:11,270
...you'll be able to tell your kids that you slept with their grandfather.

199
00:12:13,230 --> 00:12:14,600
Fine, judge all you want to.

200
00:12:14,770 --> 00:12:18,900
But married a lesbian, left a man at the altar, fell in love with a gay ice dancer...

201
00:12:19,070 --> 00:12:22,110
...threw a girl's wooden leg in the fire, live in a box.

202
00:12:29,120 --> 00:12:32,250
So, now, ahem, what exactly is the point of the box?

203
00:12:32,410 --> 00:12:34,160
Chandler?

204
00:12:34,920 --> 00:12:37,630
The meaning of the box is threefold.

205
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:42,260
One, it gives me the time to think about what I did.

206
00:12:42,420 --> 00:12:47,800
Two, it proves how much I care about my friendship with Joey.

207
00:12:47,970 --> 00:12:49,510
And three...

208
00:12:50,510 --> 00:12:52,430
...it hurts.

209
00:12:54,020 --> 00:12:55,890
- Oh, hey, hey, uh...     - Hmm?

210
00:12:56,060 --> 00:12:58,270
Remember that necklace I gave you last year?

211
00:12:58,440 --> 00:12:59,690
Can I see it?

212
00:13:00,860 --> 00:13:02,280
Why?

213
00:13:02,440 --> 00:13:04,650
I just wanna check something.

214
00:13:05,110 --> 00:13:06,530
Okay.

215
00:13:09,870 --> 00:13:11,370
Now we'll see.

216
00:13:11,540 --> 00:13:14,250
Air hole! Air hole!

217
00:13:15,790 --> 00:13:19,080
Here it is. I love it. I wear it all the time.

218
00:13:22,380 --> 00:13:25,670
The necklace I got you was gold. This is silver.

219
00:13:26,680 --> 00:13:27,720
Huh.

220
00:13:27,890 --> 00:13:30,890
Well, maybe, it, uh...

221
00:13:31,060 --> 00:13:32,720
...it changed.

222
00:13:33,560 --> 00:13:36,350
Oh, my God. You actually exchanged it.

223
00:13:36,520 --> 00:13:39,440
Isn't it better that I exchange it for something that I enjoy...

224
00:13:39,610 --> 00:13:41,360
...and I can get a lot of use out of?

225
00:13:41,520 --> 00:13:43,230
What did you get?

226
00:13:43,400 --> 00:13:45,150
Credit.

227
00:13:47,570 --> 00:13:52,240
I'll get it, I'll get it, I'll get it.

228
00:13:54,750 --> 00:13:55,790
- Hi, Tim.     - Hi.

229
00:13:55,960 --> 00:13:59,330
Hi. Thank you. Come meet my friends.

230
00:13:59,500 --> 00:14:02,630
- This is Phoebe.     - Hi, nice to meet you.

231
00:14:02,800 --> 00:14:03,840
- And Joey.     - Hey.

232
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:05,590
- Joey.     - My brother, Ross.

233
00:14:05,760 --> 00:14:06,920
- Hey.     - And Rachel.

234
00:14:07,130 --> 00:14:08,760
- Hi.     - Ahem.

235
00:14:10,800 --> 00:14:14,260
- That's Chandler.     - How do you do?

236
00:14:15,850 --> 00:14:18,180
- What's...?     - Um, well, he's, um...

237
00:14:18,350 --> 00:14:20,690
He's doing some thinking.

238
00:14:23,150 --> 00:14:24,520
He's got it.

239
00:14:24,690 --> 00:14:25,940
- Yes!     - Yeah!

240
00:14:26,110 --> 00:14:29,530
- What happened?     - You kissed my girlfriend.

241
00:14:33,740 --> 00:14:35,080
Ooh, I like those sunglasses.

242
00:14:35,620 --> 00:14:36,660
"Like them" like them...

243
00:14:36,830 --> 00:14:40,120
...or "I'd like to get store credit for that amount" like them?

244
00:14:47,420 --> 00:14:49,590
All right, everybody. This turkey is ready.

245
00:14:50,010 --> 00:14:52,340
- Where can I wash up?     - Here.

246
00:14:52,510 --> 00:14:54,100
Let me show you.

247
00:14:54,260 --> 00:14:58,310
The towels are hanging next to the sink. And you can use the fancy soap. Ha, ha.

248
00:14:58,480 --> 00:15:00,180
Thank you.

249
00:15:00,350 --> 00:15:04,110
Fancy soap? I thought we were saving that for the Pope.

250
00:15:05,270 --> 00:15:07,150
See? He's nice, right?

251
00:15:07,320 --> 00:15:11,030
Do you really wanna be in a relationship where you can actually use the phrase...

252
00:15:11,200 --> 00:15:13,320
..."That's not how your dad used to do it"?

253
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:20,710
Wow, everything looks great. Where should I sit?

254
00:15:20,870 --> 00:15:21,960
Saved you a seat.

255
00:15:22,920 --> 00:15:25,290
Sick, sick, sick.

256
00:15:27,130 --> 00:15:28,710
Oh, I'll get it.

257
00:15:28,880 --> 00:15:29,920
Gotcha.

258
00:15:33,010 --> 00:15:35,930
That doesn't sound like thinking to me.

259
00:15:36,760 --> 00:15:39,470
- Sorry.     - I don't think you should be talking at all.

260
00:15:39,640 --> 00:15:42,940
I think you got too much thinking to do to be talking and making jokes.

261
00:15:43,100 --> 00:15:44,810
Okay, okay, you got it.

262
00:15:44,980 --> 00:15:47,400
- Ross, could you pass me the yams?     - Sure.

263
00:15:47,570 --> 00:15:50,820
Oh, and Joey's got the mashed potatoes if you want to exchange them.

264
00:15:55,490 --> 00:15:57,700
Will you stop? What is the matter with you?

265
00:15:57,870 --> 00:15:59,490
Heh, heh. We've got company.

266
00:16:01,910 --> 00:16:03,830
There's nothing the matter with me.

267
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:06,210
See, I'm not completely devoid of sentiment.

268
00:16:06,380 --> 00:16:08,000
See, I have feelings.

269
00:16:08,710 --> 00:16:11,130
Okay, fine.

270
00:16:16,510 --> 00:16:21,100
You can't tell, but I'm trying to break the tension by mooning you guys.

271
00:16:26,520 --> 00:16:28,400
All right, look.

272
00:16:28,570 --> 00:16:31,650
If this is just a big joke to you, then forget about it, all right?

273
00:16:31,820 --> 00:16:33,650
This means something to me.

274
00:16:33,860 --> 00:16:36,530
If it doesn't mean anything to you, then get out of there.

275
00:16:36,700 --> 00:16:39,370
Otherwise, you're just an idiot in a box.

276
00:16:39,830 --> 00:16:42,580
You're right. I'm sorry. This means a lot to me.

277
00:16:42,750 --> 00:16:47,920
I want you to be my friend again. I swear I won't say another word tonight.

278
00:16:48,380 --> 00:16:51,250
- So you're gonna take this thing seriously?     - Absolutely.

279
00:16:51,420 --> 00:16:53,970
That sounds like another word to me.

280
00:16:54,720 --> 00:16:57,390
Are you gonna take this seriously?

281
00:17:00,930 --> 00:17:02,600
Okay.

282
00:17:04,480 --> 00:17:07,350
Don't say that I have no sentiment.

283
00:17:08,230 --> 00:17:11,440
This is a movie stub from our first date.

284
00:17:11,610 --> 00:17:15,450
This is an eggshell from the first time you made me breakfast in bed.

285
00:17:15,990 --> 00:17:20,240
This is from the museum, the first time we...

286
00:17:20,410 --> 00:17:21,870
...were together.

287
00:17:22,700 --> 00:17:28,080
Okay, maybe I exchange gifts sometimes, but I keep the things that matter.

288
00:17:28,880 --> 00:17:31,420
I don't know what to say. I'm sorry.

289
00:17:32,300 --> 00:17:34,090
Though...

290
00:17:34,260 --> 00:17:36,340
...you're not supposed to take these.

291
00:17:39,720 --> 00:17:42,640
It's like a million years old.

292
00:17:42,810 --> 00:17:46,270
We actually... We have people looking for that.

293
00:17:51,400 --> 00:17:53,020
Oh, this always happens.

294
00:17:53,570 --> 00:17:55,070
Here, let me, um...

295
00:17:55,570 --> 00:17:57,030
Thank you.

296
00:18:00,620 --> 00:18:03,240
You have very beautiful...

297
00:18:03,410 --> 00:18:05,040
...eye.

298
00:18:06,910 --> 00:18:08,660
My friends all think this is weird.

299
00:18:09,330 --> 00:18:13,460
I thought it was gonna be weird. I almost called to cancel, but it really isn't.

300
00:18:13,840 --> 00:18:17,420
I know. I mean, it's like me and your dad, that's a totally separate thing.

301
00:18:17,590 --> 00:18:18,930
Oh, I totally agree.

302
00:18:19,090 --> 00:18:22,970
I mean, we're just two people who find each other...

303
00:18:23,140 --> 00:18:25,220
...very attractive.

304
00:18:25,390 --> 00:18:26,970
Right?

305
00:18:37,690 --> 00:18:41,030
- What?     - Nothing, nothing.

306
00:18:41,200 --> 00:18:43,450
No, no, really. Oh, was that not okay?

307
00:18:43,620 --> 00:18:44,990
No, no, no, that was good.

308
00:18:45,160 --> 00:18:48,580
That was, uh... That was a good kiss.

309
00:18:49,370 --> 00:18:52,540
- Oh, my God. It didn't remind you of my...?     - Oh, don't say it.

310
00:18:53,340 --> 00:18:54,630
- But it did, didn't it?     - Yes!

311
00:18:54,800 --> 00:18:56,460
Oh, man.

312
00:18:56,630 --> 00:18:58,460
I know.

313
00:19:08,230 --> 00:19:09,810
I got it.

314
00:19:14,230 --> 00:19:15,730
Oh.

315
00:19:15,900 --> 00:19:18,610
- Hey.     - Hey.

316
00:19:18,780 --> 00:19:22,320
- I want you to know how sorry I am...     - It's okay.

317
00:19:22,490 --> 00:19:24,370
Chandler's the one I'm mad at, so...

318
00:19:24,910 --> 00:19:27,410
Well, I'm still sorry.

319
00:19:28,120 --> 00:19:31,000
- Is he here?     - In the box.

320
00:19:38,880 --> 00:19:39,920
Chandler?

321
00:19:40,090 --> 00:19:42,720
Oh, he can't talk right now.

322
00:19:43,680 --> 00:19:45,010
Why not? What's going on?

323
00:19:45,180 --> 00:19:48,220
He's trying to show Joey how much he means to him.

324
00:19:49,270 --> 00:19:52,480
- By being in a box?     - Joey had reasons.

325
00:19:54,060 --> 00:19:55,400
They were threefold.

326
00:19:57,770 --> 00:19:59,860
Oh. Well, uh...

327
00:20:00,820 --> 00:20:03,950
...you not being able to talk might actually make this easier.

328
00:20:05,530 --> 00:20:07,280
Listen, um...

329
00:20:15,790 --> 00:20:17,170
Listen.

330
00:20:17,340 --> 00:20:23,630
I don't wanna be someone who comes between two best friends.

331
00:20:23,800 --> 00:20:27,640
I just... I can't stand seeing what this is doing to you guys.

332
00:20:27,800 --> 00:20:30,600
And I don't wanna be the cause of that.

333
00:20:31,640 --> 00:20:34,140
So I don't think we can see each other anymore.

334
00:20:35,310 --> 00:20:37,730
I'm gonna go to my mom's in Chicago.

335
00:20:37,900 --> 00:20:40,570
I'm gonna stay there for a while.

336
00:20:45,610 --> 00:20:49,450
I think this could have been something really amazing.

337
00:20:49,620 --> 00:20:54,160
But, you know, this is probably for the best.

338
00:20:54,330 --> 00:20:56,170
You know?

339
00:21:01,000 --> 00:21:02,800
I'm gonna miss you.

340
00:21:05,840 --> 00:21:07,930
Goodbye, Chandler.

341
00:21:17,350 --> 00:21:20,020
Open the box.

342
00:21:20,520 --> 00:21:22,020
- What?     - He can still catch her.

343
00:21:22,190 --> 00:21:25,820
Hey, come on. Get out of there. Get out of there.

344
00:21:27,240 --> 00:21:30,120
- So...?     - Yeah, we're gonna be fine. Get out.

345
00:21:32,330 --> 00:21:33,700
- Yeah?     - Yeah.

346
00:21:33,870 --> 00:21:36,160
You did some real good thinking in there.

347
00:21:37,040 --> 00:21:38,080
I mean, this is...

348
00:21:43,050 --> 00:21:44,960
Now go. You could still catch her.

349
00:21:45,130 --> 00:21:47,880
And merry Christmas from your Secret Santa.

350
00:21:51,560 --> 00:21:54,390
All right, who got Chandler? Because I need to trade.

351
00:22:00,110 --> 00:22:02,190
Oh, he sees her.

352
00:22:02,360 --> 00:22:05,230
Aw, and he's catching up to her.

353
00:22:05,990 --> 00:22:07,900
Oh, she sees him.

354
00:22:08,280 --> 00:22:10,490
- Oh, they're hugging.     - Aw.

355
00:22:11,910 --> 00:22:14,370
He's taking her purse.

356
00:22:15,160 --> 00:22:19,370
Uh, that's not them. I'm gonna go call the police.

357
00:22:21,790 --> 00:22:23,250
- Oh, there they are.     - Where?

358
00:22:23,420 --> 00:22:24,800
- Ah!     - Oh.

359
00:22:24,960 --> 00:22:26,260
Aw.

360
00:22:30,430 --> 00:22:32,600
All right, get a room.

